# Every face vertex is written as v/vt/vn (this engine's OBJ loader
# (modelRenderer.cpp) always expects the full triplet and does not
# tolerate a bare vertex-only index). ALL v/vt/vn data is listed before
# mtllib/usemtl/f, matching how the engine's own real assets (e.g.
# Door_LeafRight.obj) are laid out -- LoadObj() fills its position/
# texcoord/normal arrays strictly in file order, so an earlier 'f' line
# would reference not-yet-read data otherwise.
# Modeled X/Z-centered with the base at local Y=0, matching key.obj's
# convention that item.cpp's Draw()/Init() math (m_Position.y - m_Scale.y,
# 0.3 uniform scale) already assumes -- no code changes needed there.
# Item_Photo.obj -- a small standing card: a dark aged-cardboard mount
# (PhotoBorder) with a lighter sepia print inset on the front (PhotoFace).
